{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-337737" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the differential equation \n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+7{y}^{′}+12y=g(x).\n$$\n\nThe corresponding homogeneous equation has the fundamental solutions ${y}_{1}(x)={e}^{-3x}$ and ${y}_{2}(x)={e}^{-4x}:$According to the method of variation of parameters, we seek a particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)={{field-1}}\n$$\n\nwhere ${u}_{1}={u}_{1}(x),{u}_{2}={u}_{2}(x),$ that satisfies the constraint\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}^{′}(x)={{field-2}}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the expressions $y={y}_{p}$ and ${y}^{′}={y}_{p}^{′}$ into the differential equation yields the following relationship between ${u}_{1}^{′},{u}_{2}^{′},$ and $g(x):$\n\n$$\n{{field-3}}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069266/state.json" "file_sha256" "3e90059d58dacbbb3ef017f422fe7274bb0423c5ee3ee46cc65f43068bcb5835"} {"question" "q-337737" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Given a second-order linear inhomogeneous differential equation, the variation of parameters method requires that we seek a particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)={u}_{1}(x){y}_{1}(x)+{u}_{2}(x){y}_{2}(x)\n$$\n\nthat satisfies the constraint\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}^{′}={u}_{1}{y}_{1}^{′}+{u}_{2}{y}_{2}^{′}.\n$$\n\nHere, ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ are linearly independent solutions of the corresponding homogeneous equation, and ${u}_{1}$ and ${u}_{2}$ are functions to be determined.\n\nIn this case, we're told that the fundamental solutions are\n\n$$\n{y}_{1}={e}^{-3x},\\,{y}_{2}={e}^{-4x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the fundamental solutions into our expression for ${y}_{p},$ we get\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}={u}_{1}{e}^{-3x}+{u}_{2}{e}^{-4x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the fundamental solutions into our constraint equation for ${y}_{p}^{′},$ we get\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}^{′}={u}_{1}({e}^{-3x})^{′}+{u}_{2}({e}^{-4x})^{′}.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $y={y}_{p}$ and ${y}^{′}={y}_{p}^{′}$ into the differential equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{″}+7{y}^{′}+12y & =g(x) \\\\ ({y}_{p}^{′})^{′}+7{y}_{p}^{′}+12{y}_{p} & =g(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing our expressions for ${y}_{p}$ and ${y}_{p}^{′},$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{({u}_{1}({e}^{-3x})^{′}+{u}_{2}({e}^{-4x})^{′})}^{′}+7({u}_{1}({e}^{-3x})^{′}+{u}_{2}({e}^{-4x})^{′})+12({u}_{1}{e}^{-3x}+{u}_{2}{e}^{-4x}) & =g(x) \\\\ {(-3{u}_{1}{e}^{-3x}-4{u}_{2}{e}^{-4x})}^{′}-21{u}_{1}{e}^{-3x}-28{u}_{2}{e}^{-4x}+12{u}_{1}{e}^{-3x}+12{u}_{2}{e}^{-4x} & =g(x) \\\\ -3{u}_{1}^{′}{e}^{-3x}+9{u}_{1}{e}^{-3x}-4{u}_{2}^{′}{e}^{-4x}+16{u}_{2}{e}^{-4x}-21{u}_{1}{e}^{-3x}-28{u}_{2}{e}^{-4x}+12{u}_{1}{e}^{-3x}+12{u}_{2}{e}^{-4x} & =g(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we group all terms proportional to ${u}_{1}$ and ${u}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1}{{(9{e}^{-3x}-21{e}^{-3x}+12{e}^{-3x})}_{⏟}}_{0}+{u}_{2}{{(16{e}^{-4x}-28{e}^{-4x}+12{e}^{-4x})}_{⏟}}_{0}-3{u}_{1}^{′}{e}^{-3x}-4{u}_{2}^{′}{e}^{-4x}=g(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that the expressions in parentheses are both zero. Therefore, the equation reduces to\n\n$$\n-3{u}_{1}^{′}{e}^{-3x}-4{u}_{2}^{′}{e}^{-4x}=g(x).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069266/state.json" "file_sha256" "3e90059d58dacbbb3ef017f422fe7274bb0423c5ee3ee46cc65f43068bcb5835"} {"question" "q-337737" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069266/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "43af5b5e073f788b6892d78fefe0bfca851fcc2333cab056e4cad4033e810668"} {"question" "q-337737" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/