gory" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069266/state.json" "file_sha256" "3e90059d58dacbbb3ef017f422fe7274bb0423c5ee3ee46cc65f43068bcb5835"} {"question" "q-337736" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-4{u}_{1}^{′}{e}^{-4x}-5{u}_{2}^{′}{e}^{-5x}=h(x)"] ["math" "-4{u}_{1}^{′}{e}^{-4x}-5{u}_{2}^{′}{e}^{-5x}={h}^{′}(x)"] ["math" "{u}_{1}^{′}{e}^{-4x}+{u}_{2}^{′}{e}^{-5x}=h(x)"] ["math" "{u}_{1}^{′}{e}^{-4x}+{u}_{2}^{′}{e}^{-5x}={h}^{′}(x)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069266/state.json" "file_sha256" "3e90059d58dacbbb3ef017f422fe7274bb0423c5ee3ee46cc65f43068bcb5835"} {"question" "q-337736" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-4{u}_{1}^{′}{e}^{-4x}-5{u}_{2}^{′}{e}^{-5x}=h(x)"] "category" "ma_explicit_answer" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069266/state.json" "file_sha256" "3e90059d58dacbbb3ef017f422fe7274bb0423c5ee3ee46cc65f43068bcb5835"} {"question" "q-337938" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the differential equation \n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-5{y}^{′}+6y={e}^{7x}.\n$$\n\nThe corresponding homogeneous equation has the fundamental solutions ${y}_{1}(x)={e}^{2x}$ and ${y}_{2}={e}^{3x}.$ \n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nAccording to the method of variation of parameters, we seek a particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)={{field-1}}\n$$\n\nwhere ${u}_{1}={u}_{1}(x),{u}_{2}={u}_{2}(x),$ that satisfies the constraint\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}^{′}(x)={{field-2}}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating ${y}_{p}$ with respect to $x,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}^{′}(x)={{field-3}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following constraint equation relating ${u}_{1}^{′}$ and ${u}_{2}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n{{field-4}}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069266/state.json" "file_sha256" "3e90059d58dacbbb3ef017f422fe7274bb0423c5ee3ee46cc65f43068bcb5835"} {"question" "q-337938" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Given a second-order linear inhomogeneous differential equation, the variation of parameters method requires that we seek a particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)={u}_{1}(x){y}_{1}(x)+{u}_{2}(x){y}_{2}(x)\n$$\n\nthat satisfies the constraint\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}^{′}={u}_{1}{y}_{1}^{′}+{u}_{2}{y}_{2}^{′}.\n$$\n\nHere, ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ are linearly independent solutions of the corresponding homogeneous equation, and ${u}_{1}$ and ${u}_{2}$ are functions to be determined.\n\nIn this case, we're told that the fundamental solutions are\n\n$$\n{y}_{1}={e}^{2x},\\,{y}_{2}={e}^{3x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the fundamental solutions into our expression for ${y}_{p},$ we get\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}={u}_{1}{e}^{2x}+{u}_{2}{e}^{3x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the fundamental solutions into our constraint equation for ${y}_{p}^{′},$ we get\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}^{′}={u}_{1}({e}^{2x})^{′}+{u}_{2}({e}^{3x})^{′}.\n$$\n\nWe can form a constraint that relates ${u}_{1}^{′}$ and ${u}_{2}^{′}$ by differentiating ${y}_{p}$ and equating this expression to our constraint on ${y}_{p}^{′}.$\n\nDifferentiating ${y}_{p}$ with respect to $x$ using the product rule, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}^{′} & ={({u}_{1}{e}^{2x}+{u}_{2}{e}^{3x})}^{′} \\\\  & ={({u}_{1}{e}^{2x})}^{′}+{({u}_{2}{e}^{3x})}^{′} \\\\  & ={u}_{1}^{′}{e}^{2x}+{u}_{1}({e}^{2x})^{′}+{u}_{2}^{′}{e}^{3x}+{u}_{2}({e}^{3x})^{′} \\\\  & ={u}_{1}^{′}{e}^{2x}+2{u}_{1}{e}^{2x}+{u}_{2}^{′}{e}^{3x}+3{u}_{2}{e}^{3x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we equate our two expressions for ${y}_{p}^{′},$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1}^{′}{e}^{2x}+2{u}_{1}{e}^{2x}+{u}_{2}^{′}{e}^{3x}+3{u}_{2}{e}^{3x} & ={u}_{1}({e}^{2x})^{′}+{u}_{2}({e}^{3x})^{′} \\\\ {u}_{1}^{′}{e}^{2x}+2{u}_{1}{e}^{2x}+{u}_{2}^{′}{e}^{3x}+3{u}_{2}{e}^{3x} & =2{u}_{1}{e}^{2x}+3{u}_{2}{e}^{3x} \\\\ {u}_{1}^{′}{e}^{2x}+\\cancel{2{u}_{1}{e}^{2x}}+{u}_{2}^{′}{e}^{3x}+\\cancel{3{u}_{2}{e}^{3x}} & =\\cancel{2{u}_{1}{e}^{2x}}+\\cancel{3{u}_{2}{e}^{3x}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich finally gives\n\n$$\n{u}_{1}^{′}{e}^{2x}+{u}_{2}^{′}{e}^{3x}=0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069266/state.json" "file_sha256" "3e90059d58dacbbb3ef017f422fe7274bb0423c5ee3ee46cc65f43068bcb5835"} {"question" "q-337938" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069266/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "43af5b5e073f788b6892d78fefe0bfca851fcc2333cab056e4cad4033e810668"} {"question" "q-337938" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069266/state.json" "file_sha256" "3e90059d58dacbbb3ef017f422fe7274bb0423c5ee3ee46cc65f43068bcb5835"} {"question" "q-337938" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{u}_{1}({e}^{2x})^{′}+{u}_{2}({e}^{3x})^{′}"] ["math" "{u}_{1}^{′}({e}^{2x})^{′}+{u}_{2}^{′}({e}^{3x})^{′}"] ["math" "{u}_{1}^{′}{e}^{2x}+{u}_{2}^{′}{e}^{3x}"] ["math" "{u}_{1}{e}^{2x}+{u}_{2}{e}^{3x}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069266/state.json" "file_sha256" "3e90059d58dacbbb3ef017f422fe7274bb0423c5ee3ee46cc65f43068bcb5835"} {"question" "q-337938" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{u}_{1}{e}^{2x}+{u}_{2}{e}^{3x}"] "category" "ma_explicit_answer" "file"