ame{cos}⁡(2x).\n$$\n\nSubstituting the fundamental solutions into our constraint equation for ${y}_{p}^{′},$ we get\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}^{′}={u}_{1}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x))^{′}+{u}_{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x))^{′}.\n$$\n\nWe can form a constraint that relates ${u}_{1}^{′}$ and ${u}_{2}^{′}$ by differentiating ${y}_{p}$ and equating this expression to our constraint on ${y}_{p}^{′}.$\n\nDifferentiating ${y}_{p}$ with respect to $x$ using the product rule, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}^{′} & ={({u}_{1}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+{u}_{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x))}^{′} \\\\  & ={({u}_{1}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x))}^{′}+{({u}_{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x))}^{′} \\\\  & ={u}_{1}^{′}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+{u}_{1}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x))^{′}+{u}_{2}^{′}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+{u}_{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x))^{′} \\\\  & ={u}_{1}^{′}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+2{u}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+{u}_{2}^{′}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)-2{u}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we equate our two expressions for ${y}_{p}^{′},$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1}^{′}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+2{u}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+{u}_{2}^{′}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)-2{u}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x) & ={u}_{1}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x))^{′}+{u}_{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x))^{′} \\\\ {u}_{1}^{′}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+2{u}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+{u}_{2}^{′}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)-2{u}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x) & =2{u}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)-2{u}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x) \\\\ {u}_{1}^{′}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+\\cancel{2{u}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}+{u}_{2}^{′}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)-\\cancel{2{u}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)} & =\\cancel{2{u}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}-\\cancel{2{u}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich finally gives\n\n$$\n{u}_{1}^{′}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+{u}_{2}^{′}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)=0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-captur